/A$, not $/A^2$. Either the volume scales as A^2, or the normalisation is by something other than volume (pair count C(A,2) ~ A^2/2 would give A^2 directly and is the likelier intent). As written the justification contradicts the exponent it justifies.","history":2},{"id":"trap-em-dash","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e02","history":2},{"id":"trap-meta-commentary","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e02","history":2},{"id":"trap-negation-contrast","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e02","history":2},{"id":"trap-nonspeakable","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e02","history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e02","history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e02","history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e02","history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e02","history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e02","history":2},{"id":"uses-editorial-hygiene","group":"uses","result":"warn","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","history":1},{"id":"uses-formal-coverage","group":"uses","result":"n/a","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-08-09